Map data (standby city map)
---------------------------

OpenStreetMap — Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0
  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
  The optional standby city map is generated on the Hauser server from
  OpenStreetMap road geometry. When a location is configured, the server queries
  a public Overpass API endpoint once and renders a monochrome SVG of road lines
  into its own data directory. Map data is © OpenStreetMap contributors and is
  available under the ODbL; a produced SVG is a derived database extract, so the
  same terms apply to it.

  One such extract IS bundled with this repository:
    `app/public/assets/ambient-maps/`
  It holds a single pre-rendered example map shown in the setup wizard, so that
  the feature can be previewed before any location is sent anywhere. It is
  derived from OpenStreetMap data and carries the ODbL like any other extract.
  No OpenStreetMap code is included or depended upon.

  Place search uses OpenStreetMap's Nominatim geocoder. What leaves the server
  is a search term, never a stored address.

Overpass API — the public query service
  https://overpass-api.de/ and https://overpass.kumi.systems/
  Hauser sends only a bounding box and a road-type filter, and only when
  someone sets or regenerates the location. No Overpass or OpenStreetMap code
  is included or depended upon; the query is a plain HTTPS request made by the
  server.


