Attribution placement
---------------------
The OpenStreetMap credit is shown in Hauser's settings (Appearance > Ambient &
Standby) and in this file, not on the standby screen itself. The standby screen
is a purely decorative surface with no controls, and the map is rendered as a
low-opacity mask behind the clock. OpenStreetMap's attribution guidelines allow
a produced work that is not a browsable map to carry its credit where credits
are customarily found rather than inside the image. The credit is therefore
placed where it stays legible and reachable instead of being reduced to an
unreadable line on a wall panel.
